-- the T separator is a separator and nothing more
ok   T parses            
ok   and agrees with space

-- Z is UTC, so the civil fields already ARE the answer
ok   Z is a no-op        
ok   with a space too    
ok   +00:00 likewise     

-- a non-zero offset converts to UTC, and the SIGN is the whole point
ok   +02:00 goes BACK    
ok   -05:00 goes FORWARD 

-- the compact spellings of the same offset agree
ok   +0200               
ok   +02                 

-- IT IS DATE ARITHMETIC, NOT HOUR SUBTRACTION
ok   crosses a year      
ok   and a month         

-- lower precisions keep theirs
ok   minute precision    
ok   hour precision      

-- CONTROLS: a bare date ends in `-07` and is NOT an offset
ok   a bare date         
ok   month precision     
ok   year precision      

-- CONTROLS: and the refusals, so this is not `accept anything`
ok   a zone with no time 
ok   an impossible offset
ok   a bare sign         
ok   trailing junk       
ok   some other letter   
